<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2013/05/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>Beckhoff-USA-Community.XAE.TcCom.AdsGamepad</id>
    <version>0.0.0.11</version>
    <title>ADS Gamepad TcCOM Module</title>
    <authors>Beckhoff Automation LLC</authors>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/Beckhoff-USA-Community/ADS-Gamepad-Service</projectUrl>
    <copyright>(c) Beckhoff Automation LLC</copyright>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>true</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <license type="file">LICENSE.txt</license>
    <readme>docs/README.md</readme>
    <summary>Compiled Gamepad TcCOM module for the ADS Gamepad Service</summary>
    <tags>Beckhoff TwinCAT</tags>
    <description>The compiled and signed Gamepad TcCOM module, a TwinCAT C++ module that reads a controller from the ADS Gamepad Service and exposes it as process data with no PLC code involved. The package installs the module into the TwinCAT module repository under C:\ProgramData\Beckhoff\TwinCAT\3.1\Repository, so it is ready to add to a project right after the install. Builds are included for TwinCAT RT x86 and x64, for TwinCAT OS x64, and for Beckhoff RT Linux x64 as a TME file that the target loads without signing. The source lives in the project repository for anyone who prefers to build and sign the module themselves.</description>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="repository\**" target="tools\repository" />
    <file src="docs\README.md" target="docs\README.md" />
    <file src="tools\chocolateyinstall.ps1" target="tools\chocolateyinstall.ps1" />
    <file src="tools\chocolateyuninstall.ps1" target="tools\chocolateyuninstall.ps1" />
    <file src="LICENSE.txt" target="LICENSE.txt" />
  </files>
</package>
